From: "Jonas (via Claude)" <jonas@insidia.de>
Date: Wed, 27 May 2026 07:23:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat: add Grok Build agent support (xAI CLI)

Adds grok-build as a new agent provider in Maestro's pluggable architecture.

Scaffolding (CI-gated, agent-completeness test passes):
- Agent ID 'grok-build' in AGENT_IDS tuple
- AgentConfig with -p prompt delivery, streaming-json output, permission modes
- 25 capability flags (batch, streaming, resume, model selection, group chat)
- Display name, PLAN_MODE_AGENTS, BETA_AGENTS registration
- Default context window 131k (configurable up to 2M for Grok 4 Heavy)

Output parser (grok-build-output-parser.ts, 31 tests):
- Handles init, text delta, thinking/reasoning, tool use, result events
- Usage stats with reasoning token tracking (Grok 4 Heavy)
- Flexible field fallbacks (delta/content/text) for schema resilience

Error patterns (6 categories):
- auth_expired, token_exhaustion, rate_limited, network_error
- agent_crashed, permission_denied (incl. sandbox-specific messages)

Config options:
- Model selection (grok-4.3, grok-4-heavy, etc.)
- Context window override
- Sandbox profile (workspace/off/strict) for OSINT network egress

NOTE: Event type constants in the parser are best-effort pending real
streaming-json output verification. Run:
  grok -p "say hello" --output-format streaming-json 2>&1 | head -50
Then update constants in grok-build-output-parser.ts (grep TODO).
